Archive source fixtures for tests/archive-source-listing-keys.test.ts
=====================================================================

Every file is a real container of its format, written by a tool other than 7-Zip (the tool under test reads
them; it never produced them). Built on Ubuntu 24.04. 7-Zip 23.01 and p7zip 16.02 both list every file with
keys inside the whitelist in src/lib/conversions/archive-extraction-safety.ts.

Common payload (WORK/src), timestamps set to 2024-01-02 03:04:06 with `touch -d`:

  hello.txt        "hello archive\n"                     (14 bytes)
  dir/nested.txt   "nested file\n"                       (12 bytes)
  dir/data.bin     bytes 0x00..0xFF in order             (256 bytes)

The test regenerates these literals; it never reads the expected bytes back from an extraction.
`generators/` holds the scripts and spec for the hand-assembled formats and the RPM.

